# .env.example
#
# Sample overrides for the local RAG system. Defaults live in .env.default;
# this file only shows what you can change and why you might want to.
#
# To use it:
#   cp .env.example .env
# then uncomment the lines you want. Anything you leave commented keeps its
# value from .env.default. Never commit .env.
#
# You can also override a single setting for one run from the shell:
#   LLM_MODEL=qwen3:4b python -m src.app

# --- Use a smaller, faster chat model ----------------------------------------
# Good for laptops without much RAM or a GPU. Run `ollama pull qwen3:4b` first.
# LLM_MODEL=qwen3:4b

# --- Allow more varied answers -----------------------------------------------
# LLM_TEMPERATURE=0.7

# --- Fit more retrieved context into each prompt -----------------------------
# Send more chunks per question, and give the model enough room for them.
# RETRIEVAL_K=6
# LLM_CONTEXT_WINDOW=16384

# --- Use Ollama running on another machine -----------------------------------
# On that machine, start Ollama with OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0 so it accepts
# connections from the network.
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://192.168.1.50:11434

# --- Try a different embedding model -----------------------------------------
# Run `ollama pull mxbai-embed-large` first. Vectors from different models
# can't be mixed, so point VECTORSTORE_PATH at a new folder (or delete the
# old store) before ingesting.
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=mxbai-embed-large
# VECTORSTORE_PATH=data/vectorstore-mxbai

# --- Keep a separate document set and index ----------------------------------
# Useful for switching between projects without re-ingesting each time.
# DOCUMENTS_PATH=/Users/me/Documents/research-papers
# VECTORSTORE_PATH=data/vectorstore-research

# --- Larger chunks for long-form documents -----------------------------------
# Chunk IDs don't encode the chunk settings, so use a new VECTORSTORE_PATH
# (or delete the old store) before ingesting with different values.
# CHUNK_SIZE=2000
# CHUNK_OVERLAP=400
# VECTORSTORE_PATH=data/vectorstore-2000

# --- Gentler ingestion when Ollama struggles ---------------------------------
# Smaller embedding batches if Ollama errors or runs out of memory.
# EMBEDDING_BATCH_SIZE=8
